WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Linux agents edit evaluation code and run tests. Windows cycles through planning, creating slides, receiving and sending email, and analyzing dashboards. All activity is simulated.

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
Linux pushes tested code to the cloud over SSH or through GitHub Actions. Cloud GPUs preprocess dataset shards, train a model, and run evaluation. Large data stays in the cloud.

00:16.000 --> 00:24.000
Read available usage records from local .claude and .codex directories. Linux pulls cloud logs over SSH and relays them to Windows. Windows also ingests its own usage logs. Verify, deduplicate, and preserve project IDs.

00:24.000 --> 00:32.000
At 00:15 Seoul, close the previous day and accumulate tokens by project and model. Late records revise totals. Missing or offline sources remain visibly incomplete.

00:32.000 --> 00:40.000
Monday at 08:00 Seoul, combine seven daily ledgers, review the project and model split, link verified progress, and suggest optimizations. Example weekly usage is 4.10 million agent tokens; cloud compute costs are separate.
